# `arvo-numeral`: a value of a declared signature, held in its derived carrier

Canon this design declares:
`ruling::the_format_spine_is_canon`, for the sum, the difference, the negation, the product, the
quotient and the conversion the value computes, each the format's own.
`ruling::behaviour_is_stated_per_declared_signature_and_the_premise_dissolves`, for the carrier being
observable through the host's layout and through nothing the value declares.
`ruling::the_derivation_is_a_placement_and_the_operation_set_is_an_admission_rule`, for the admission.
`ruling::the_overflow_panic_is_permitted_and_bounded` and `ruling::never_a_runtime_check_and_one_lowered_path`,
for the debug check, an axis of its own that defaults to the abort.
`obligation::a_platform_sized_unsigned_integer_at_an_api_position` and
`obligation::a_primitive_for_every_position_a_bare_number_would_take`, for the aliases.
`ruling::behaviour_is_stated_per_declared_signature_and_the_premise_dissolves` and
`ruling::the_derivation_is_a_placement_and_the_operation_set_is_an_admission_rule` again, as the licence
for a value type at all: both presuppose a sized type holding one value at sole occupancy. That clause as
a statement of its own is open, with one cold read so far.
`ruling::a_format_datum_is_one_point_and_a_saturating_end_is_one_point`, for what the value holds: one
point of the format's ambient domain.
`proposal::a_value_is_the_sole_occupancy_placement_of_a_declared_signature`, at one expert, which this
crate builds on and does not promote. Where it says more than that ruling, its slot and its one canonical
encoding, this crate takes the same choice as its own, under `question::what_a_datum_stands_for`.
`proposal::a_missing_identity_is_refused_as_a_failed_constant`, at one expert, for the shape both
identities take, built on and not promoted.
`ruling::the_debug_abort_is_configured_by_the_consumer`, op's direction that the consumer chooses the
abort, and `proposal::the_debug_check_is_a_parameter_the_consumer_names`, at one expert, for the vehicle.
`obligation::a_deterministic_fixed_point_lane_with_declared_rounding`, for the fixed-point aliases,
whose rounding the consumer declares.
